==Battleground==
*1 [[Spacefish Jones]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*3 [[Project A]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*5 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[General GreGory]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[General GreGory]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*1 [[General GreGory]] spawns after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]], this stage is a complete and utter joke and is the easiest stage that derives from [[First Round (Deadly)]]. Without any [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]], this stage is near impossible. With only the ones from [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 1, this stage is a force to be reckoned with, the General GreGories have nearly 500,000 HP and about 35,000 DPS, making everything just about still impossible for how early on they spawn, not even mentioning the Project As and Spacefish Jones. This stage is meant to be played with Cats of the Cosmos Chapter 2 and above [[Treasure]]s, so keep that in mind.

You should have [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] units in your lineup, as [[3rd Round: Dawn (Deadly)]] also has [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies in it, but if you don't, its fine as long as you have all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] so you can basically spawn whatever is in your lineup. When doing this stage with Cats of the Cosmos Chapter 1 & 2 [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]], just spawn anti-Alien cats like [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] / [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], and just use [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and/or other [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rushers]] for the Project As and Spacefish Jones.

